    "text": "The eel is a symbolic animal in Irish lore. Fish play little part in Celtic legend except the salmon, yet the eel appears often in Ireland. Eels were plentiful food during the spring migration. People believed they grew from horsehairs left too long in water. Folklore held that eels could reincarnate. Some eels traveled across land to graveyards and ate corpses. A monster eel, an ollipheist or eascú, rose near Liscannor in County Clare. The goddess Mórrígan took eel form before the hero Cúchulainn. The monstrous Caoránach dwelt in Lough Derg.",
